  "summary": "Climate and health exchange map with watershed context, health facilities, future heat rasters, and precipitation-change layers.",
  "sourceNote": "Climate surfaces reproduce the original Northern Health consultant archive: annual days above 29°C (P50, SSP585, BCCAQv2 CMIP6) and future-minus-past seasonal precipitation in mm. Exact numeric vector blocks retain the original continuous QGIS colour ramps. The Northern Health outline uses the shared BCMoH vector; watershed boundaries and hospitals use local PGMaps vectors. River and watershed-label context still uses the Nechako portal.",
  "details": [
    "Created for the NH - UNBC Climate & Health Knowledge Exchange Event on April 12, 2024.",
    "The project gives Northern Health staff and UNBC researchers a shared map package for climate-health discussion, northern BC expertise, resources, and collaboration opportunities.",
    "The consultant archive contains P50, SSP585 ClimateData.ca BCCAQv2 CMIP6 surfaces clipped to Northern Health. Heat uses days above 29°C for 1971–2000 and 2071–2100; this differs from the live portal’s >30°C layer. Seasonal precipitation is the change in total mm between those periods."
  ],
